<div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
  <p>A desk HUD built from a 1.28" round GC9A01 display and an ESP32-S3-Zero, fed over USB.</p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>A Swift menu bar app on the Mac renders every frame, previews it in its popover, and sends it to the board as a JPEG. The ESP32 firmware just receives, decodes and draws, so changing the design never needs a reflash.</p>
</div>
